Eighteen months. Each month the process finds the worst cell and
'intervenes' -- an intervention with a TRUE EFFECT OF ZERO.

Cells are split by automation.assign -- deterministic in the cell's
own key, so a replay makes the same assignments as the live run.

  group     n   mean fall     mean bounce    apparent recovery
  treated   12  -7106         3458           48.7%
  holdout   5   -8431         7208           85.5%

  WHAT WE LEARNED, measured the obvious way:
    the intervention recovers 48.7% of the loss.

  That is the number a learning loop would store, and it is FALSE.
  The intervention does nothing. What it measures is REGRESSION TO
  THE MEAN: a cell is picked BECAUSE it was extreme, and extreme
  observations contain noise, which does not repeat.

  WHAT WE LEARNED, against the holdout:
    treated recovered  48.7%
    holdout recovered  85.5%
    effect of acting   -36.8%

  The cells nobody touched recovered just as well. THAT is the
  measurement, and it needs something the system had no concept of:
  occasions on which it deliberately did NOT act.

  And note what the honest conclusion is NOT. The difference is
  small on a handful of observations either way, which is not a
  measurement of anything -- it is noise, and a holdout this
  small cannot resolve a small effect either. The defensible
  statement is that there is no evidence the intervention does
  anything, which happens to be exactly right: it does nothing.

  Recipe 5 ASSUMED a recovery of 60% and warned that its
  recommendation was sensitive to it. This is where that number was
  going to come from, and uncontrolled it would have come back 52%.
